	('richard', 'developer-stats', 'txt', 1, '327ea31f-2d3e-454c-b921-bb32d3bdfd4d', '', '', '', '', '', 'kwk', 'c4a7f65f-efeb-11e6-a9bf-7831c1d422a2', 0, '', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855', '', false, false, '', false, 'map[addr:[::1]:50116 v:v0.8.19+50954ce host:Richards-MacBook-Pro.local os:darwin agnt:<not implemented>]', false, 0, 1501192749155, 1501192749155, 1501192749155, ''),
	('richard', 'developer-stats', 'txt', 2, '327ea31f-2d3e-454c-b921-bb32d3bdfd4d', '', '', '', '', '', 'kwk', 'c4a7f65f-efeb-11e6-a9bf-7831c1d422a2', 0, 'Number of go devs: 500k-1mil: https://research.swtch.com/gophercount?utm_source=golangweekly&utm_medium=email', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'bee0ba4db7e83127f0980e7e11997498c312ec4562c0f71a3d1a41e099f35fda', '', false, false, '', true, '', false, 0, 1501192768539, 1501192768539, 1501192768539, ''),
	('richard', 'devenv', 'sh', 2, '85310cf0-ccb5-11e6-8e2a-27249dd1b81b', '', '', '', '', '', 'kwk', 'c4a7f65f-efeb-11e6-a9bf-7831c1d422a2', 0, 'export KWK_TEST_MODE=true', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '60ade6f583a9c5a720509db7e35896cb24b057d7cd6b4e166f072cc952be5498', '', false, false, '', true, 'cass', false, 0, 1487036716228, 1495404779293, 0, ''),
	('richard', 'devserve', 'sh', 1, '55499cb7-092a-11e7-9116-7831c1d422a2', '', '', '', '', '', 'kwk', 'c4a7f65f-efeb-11e6-a9bf-7831c1d422a2', 0, 'CASS_HOST_IP=localhost:9042 ./src', '', '', 2, 1489546325000, 0, 0, 0, '5959392881a894819f773c80c6b641ca4a7d87898746c64909e0f9117c4b7432', '', false, false, '', false, 'cass', true, 1499154602353, 1489546308225, 1495404777790, 0, e': line 2: ./src: No such file or directory\x1b[0m'),
	('richard', 'edit-models', 'txt', 1, '9e264cd0-01d1-4eee-b66a-1b9f2745c64d', '', '', '', '', '', 'kwk', 'c4a7f65f-efeb-11e6-a9bf-7831c1d422a2', 0, e'Guiding Principals\n\n\n\n==== \'git\' model\n\nCase: draft\n1. Check that the file exists on disk.\n2. If yes then open that.\n3. User edits file as they would.\n4. User must commit to save changes to cloud.\n\nCase: fresh edit\n1. No existing file on disk\n2. Get file from cloud\n3. See above\n\nPros:\n- Known workflow\n- Flexible \n- Versions are explicit\n- Gives chance to try something as a draft e.g. running the snippet\n\nCons: \n- more commands (commit)\n- UI needs to have \'draft\' flags and management\n\n==== \'opaque\' model\n1. Get file from cloud every time.\n2. Terminal waits for edit completion.\n3. User edits file.\n4. User confirms commit to waiting terminal.\n\nPros:\n- No draft state, less things to think about.\n- feels quick\nCons:\n- Heavy weight creating a version for each edit\n- A bit clumsy if you don\'t do all your changes in one session\n\n=== \'flexi opaque\' LESS INVASIVE\nSame as opaque but no terminal wait, save command added upload edits:\n    - drafts folder will list all edited files that don\'t match remote versions. \n    - \'save\' will upload commit and push all drafts. (expect to be used most)\n    - \'save <name>\' will just commit a specific file.\n    - kwk unsaved\n    - kwk rm unsaved will remove all local changes (but keep originals)\n    - kwk signout will remove all unsaved local changes.\n\nPros:\n- Keeps existing model but allows flexible committing.\nCons:\n- Extra command\n- Extra folder\n\n\n==== \'quiet\' model (File Sync Model) INVASIVE\n1. Open existing file or get from cloud.\n2. User makes changes\n3. Sho3. Sho3. Sho3. Sho h3. Sho3. Sho3. Sho3. Sho h3. Sho3tly\n4. Daemon lives for 10 mins then closes.\n5. No versions\n\n\n. No versions\n for 10 mins then closes.\nShvenShve snippets without using the cli\nCons:\n- More complex sync, kind of like a dropbox model\n- File name formats and \n\n', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '50a5d23a745a17b075159161c408f13c833bfbec427531d10d7690cf0993f4bd', '', false, false, '', false, 'map[os:darwin agnt:<not implemented> addr:[::1]:58068 v:v0.8.19+50954ce host:Richards-MacBook-Pro.local]', false, 0, 1502057531523, 1502057531523, 1502057531523, ''),
	('richard', 'edit-models', 'txt', 2, '9e264cd0-01d1-4eee-b66a-1b9f2745c64d', '', '', '', '', '', 'kwk', 'c4a7f65f-efeb-11e6-a9bf-7831c1d422a2', 0, e'Guiding Principals\n\n=== \'inline only\' model\nGiven the purpose of quick is to avoid context switching then perhaps its better to only allow inline editing. Thus vim, emacs, nano and micro are supported. After all you only need a simple editor for snippets? Also micro could be integrated with kwk.\n\n\n==== \'git\' model\n\nCase: draft\n1. Check that the file exists on disk.\n2. If yes then open that.\n3. User edits file as they would.\n4. User must commit to save changes to cloud.\n\nCase: fresh edit\n1. No existing file on disk\n2. Get file from cloud\n3. See above\n\nPros:\n- Known workflow\n- Flexible \n- Versions are explicit\n- Gives chance to try something as a draft e.g. running the snippet\n\nCons: \n- more commands (commit)\n- UI needs to have \'draft\' flags and management\n\n==== \'opaque\' model\n1. Get file from cloud every time.\n2. Terminal waits for edit completion.\n3. User edits file.\n4. User confirms commit to waiting terminal.\n\nPros:\n- No draft state, less things to think about.\n- feels quick\nCons:\n- Heavy weight creating a version for each edit\n- A bit clumsy if you don\'t do all your changes in one session\n\n=== \'flexi opaque\' LESS INVASIVE\nSame as opaque but no terminal wait, save command added upload edits:\n    - drafts folder will list all edited files that don\'t match remote versions. \n    - \'save\' will upload commit and push all drafts. (expect to be used most)\n    - \'save <name>\' will just commit a specific file.\n    - kwk unsaved\n    - kwk rm unsaved will remove all local changes (but keep originals)\n    - kwk signout will remove all unsaved local changes.\n\nPros:\n- Keeps existing model but allows flexible committing.\nCons:\n- Extra command\n- Extra folder\n\n\n==== \'quiet\' model (File Sync Model) INVASIVE\n1. Open existing file or get from cloud.\n2. User makes changes\n3. Sho3. Sho3. Sho3. Sho h3. Sho3. Sho3. Sho3. Sho h3. Sho3tly\n4. Daemon lives for 10 mins then closes.\n5. No versions\n\n\n. No versions\n for 10 mins then closes.\nShvenShve snippets without using the cli\nCons:\n- More complex sync, kind of like a dropbox model\n- File name formats and ', '', '', 1, 1502145514589, 0, 1, 0, 'de6799bd54664f7b7a4e225ae1013de2b3fc87af0add2594a93efba5ab1d085f', '', false, false, '', false, '', false, 0, 1502145508145, 1502145508145, 1502145514589, e'\x1b[0m'),
	('richard', 'edit-models', 'txt', 3, '9e264cd0-01d1-4eee-b66a-1b9f2745c64d', '', '', '', '', '', 'kwk', 'c4a7f65f-efeb-11e6-a9bf-7831c1d422a2', 0, e'Guiding Principals\n\n=== \'streaming model\'\nWhilst editing you can flick back to the terminal and press any key to persist changes. It will only create a new version when you exit the streamer. When you\'re done you can stop listening by pressing ctrl+c or q.\n\n- Or whilst editing the streamer is actually checking for changes as you save the file, you can quit when you like and only then will it create a new version and stop listening. To resume streaming type \'kwk edit again\' and it will pick up from where it left off. To avoid having to stream you can just type \'kwk save\'.\n\n=== \'inline only\' model\nGiven the purpose of quick is to avoid context switching then perhaps its better to only allow inline editing. Thus vim, emacs, nano and micro are supported. After all you only need a simple editor for snippets? Also micro could be integrated with kwk.\n\n\n==== \'git\' model\n\nCase: draft\n1. Check that the file exists on disk.\n2. If yes then open that.\n3. User edits file as they would.\n4. User must commit to save changes to cloud.\n\nCase: fresh edit\n1. No existing file on disk\n2. Get file from cloud\n3. See above\n\nPros:\n- Known workflow\n- Flexible \n- Versions are explicit\n- Gives chance to try something as a draft e.g. running the snippet\n\nCons: \n- more commands (commit)\n- UI needs to have \'draft\' flags and management\n\n==== \'opaque\' model\n1. Get file from cloud every time.\n2. Terminal waits for edit completion.\n3. User edits file.\n4. User confirms commit to waiting terminal.\n\nPros:\n- No draft state, less things to think about.\n- feels quick\nCons:\n- Heavy weight creating a version for each edit\n- A bit clumsy if you don\'t do all your changes in one session\n\n=== \'flexi opaque\' LESS INVASIVE\nSame as opaque but no terminal wait, save command added upload edits:\n    - drafts folder will list all edited files that don\'t match remote versions. \n    - \'save\' will upload commit and push all drafts. (expect to be used most)\n    - \'save <name>\' will just commit a specific file.\n    - kwk unsaved\n    - kwk rm unsaved will remove all local changes (but keep originals)\n    - kwk signout will remove all unsaved local changes.\n\nPros:\n- Keeps existing model but allows flexible committing.\nCons:\n- Extra command\n- Extra folder\n\n\n==== \'quiet\' model (File Sync Model) INVASIVE\n1. Open existing file or get from cloud.\n2. User makes changes\n3. Sho3. Sho3. Sho3. Sho h3. Sho3. Sho3. Sho3. Sho h3. Sho3tly\n4. Daemon lives for 10 mins then closes.\n5. No versions\n\n\n. No versions\n for 10 mins then closes.\nShvenShve snippets without using the cli\nCons:\n- More complex sync, kind of like a dropbox model\n- File name formats and ', '', '', 1, 1502145514589, 0, 0, 0, 'f49760223ff22582b434ac260615fa4b479f255916a454aa6a71bec6e4234527', '', false, false, '', false, '', false, 0, 1502145914062, 1502145914062, 1502145914062, e'\x1b[0m'),
