itions:\nhttp://datagenetics.com/blog/november42012/index.html\n\nSuggestion based on dictionary:\nhttps://github.com/sajari/fuzzy\n- which dictionary? Could be used for snippet names', '', '', 1, 1500681027187, 0, 0, 0, '1543efcfca106a0aaa3c45e2a84147ac72514327b00c6670e416345b648a102a', '', true, false, '', false, '', false, 0, 1500690655543, 1500756269735, 1500756269735, e'\x1b[0m'),
	('richard', 'algos', 'txt', 13, 'dcf675ee-f1ab-448b-ab6c-d60165969965', '', '', '', '', '', 'learn', '94b78f43-b593-4b17-b5a7-3137ce198216', 0, e'// BLOOM\nhttps://github.com/tylertreat/BoomFilters\n- tunable\n\ngithub.com/yourbasic/bloom\n - many false positives, not tenable\n\nhttps://github.com/dataence/bloom\n- no viewed\n\nhttps://github.com/seiflotfy/cuckoofilter\n\n// BITSETS in go\nhttps://github.com/willf/bitset\n(intersections etc with bit sets unlike math big)\n\nDATA STRUCTURES\nhttps://github.com/Workiva/go-datastructures\n- includes b-trees sets etc\n\nhttps://github.com/emirpasic/gods#hashset\n\n// Rabin-karp\ngithub.com/glkz/rabinkarp\n- Returns the strings it finds - want the indices rather\n\n// Maths for com sci\nhttps://ocw.mit.edu/courses/electrical-engineering-and-computer-science/6-042j-mathematics-for-computer-science-spring-2015/index.htm\n\nLevenstein\nhttps://github.com/agext/levenshtein\nLevenstein automata\nhttp://blog.notdot.net/2010/07/Damn-Cool-Algorithms-Levenshtein-Automata\n- Search a regular index in a fuzzy manner\nhttps://github.com/junegunn/fzf/tree/master/src\nfzf - fuzzy cli search (levenstein) \n\nTrie\nhttps://github.com/derekparker/trie\n- Fast fuzzy search\n- Trie is a compact way to store text\n\n// Coursera course\nhttps://www.coursera.org/specializations/algorithms?action=enroll\n\nCode Search\n// Search over code using indexed files\nhttps://github.com/google/codesearch\n//\nhttps://github.com/monochromegane/the_platinum_searcher\n- Could use to create highlights?\n- Also be interesting to see how fast it is (since it uses regex)\n\nSimilarity checking:\nhttps://github.com/dgryski/go-simstore\n- Used for web indexing pages which are Not similar\nhttp://www2007.org/papers/paper215.pdf\n\nExtract urls from text\nhttps://github.com/mvdan/xurls\n\nFuzz can be fake by search exact and then using a dictionary to search for other terms:\n  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commonly_misspelled_English_words \nCommon key transpositions:\nhttp://datagenetics.com/blog/november42012/index.html\n\nSuggestion based on dictionary:\nhttps://github.com/sajari/fuzzy\n- which dictionary? Could be used for snippet names\n\n// Inverted index\n\nCREATE TABLE `index` (\n  `id` int(11) unsigned NOT NULL,\n  `token` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `ext` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `line` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `pos` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `type` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `o_token` varchar(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=latin1;\n\ntruncate `index`;\ninsert into `index` (`id`, `name`, `ext`, `token`, `line`, `pos`, `type`, `o_token`) values\n(4, \'tmap\', \'txt\', \'unicode\', 2, 20, 1, null),\n(5, \'tmap\', \'txt\', \'print\', 2, 15, 1, null),\n(6, \'tmap\', \'txt\', \'1F680\', 2, 25, 1, null);\n\nselect * from `index` where token regexp \'unicide|unicode|unocode\'', '', '', 1, 1500792464170, 0, 6, 0, 'bfddbe8c8f1bdb76c863aee39124fe847cfcf92be9ad215a96bee118ca3a9c49', '', true, false, '', false, '', false, 0, 1500691050005, 1500756269735, 1500792464170, e'\x1b[0m'),
	('richard', 'algos', 'txt', 14, 'dcf675ee-f1ab-448b-ab6c-d60165969965', '', '', '', '', '', 'learn', '94b78f43-b593-4b17-b5a7-3137ce198216', 0, e'// BLOOM\nhttps://github.com/tylertreat/BoomFilters\n- tunable\n\ngithub.com/yourbasic/bloom\n - many false positives, not tenable\n\nhttps://github.com/dataence/bloom\n- no viewed\n\nhttps://github.com/seiflotfy/cuckoofilter\n\n// BITSETS in go\nhttps://github.com/willf/bitset\n(intersections etc with bit sets unlike math big)\n\nDATA STRUCTURES\nhttps://github.com/Workiva/go-datastructures\n- includes b-trees sets etc\n\nhttps://github.com/emirpasic/gods#hashset\n\n// Rabin-karp\ngithub.com/glkz/rabinkarp\n- Returns the strings it finds - want the indices rather\n\n// Maths for com sci\nhttps://ocw.mit.edu/courses/electrical-engineering-and-computer-science/6-042j-mathematics-for-computer-science-spring-2015/index.htm\n\nLevenstein\nhttps://github.com/agext/levenshtein\nLevenstein automata\nhttp://blog.notdot.net/2010/07/Damn-Cool-Algorithms-Levenshtein-Automata\n- Search a regular index in a fuzzy manner\nhttps://github.com/junegunn/fzf/tree/master/src\nfzf - fuzzy cli search (levenstein) \n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Approximate_string_matching\n- says we can do levenstein at O(m+n), seems a bit dubious)\n\nTrie\nhttps://github.com/derekparker/trie\n- Fast fuzzy search\n- Trie is a compact way to store text\n\n// Coursera course\nhttps://www.coursera.org/specializations/algorithms?action=enroll\n\nCode Search\n// Search over code using indexed files\nhttps://github.com/google/codesearch\n//\nhttps://github.com/monochromegane/the_platinum_searcher\n- Could use to create highlights?\n- Also be interesting to see how fast it is (since it uses regex)\n\nSimilarity checking:\nhttps://github.com/dgryski/go-simstore\n- Used for web indexing pages which are Not similar\nhttp://www2007.org/papers/paper215.pdf\n\nExtract urls from text\nhttps://github.com/mvdan/xurls\n\nFuzz can be fake by search exact and then using a dictionary to search for other terms:\n  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commonly_misspelled_English_words \nCommon key transpositions:\nhttp://datagenetics.com/blog/november42012/index.html\n\nSuggestion based on dictionary:\nhttps://github.com/sajari/fuzzy\n- which dictionary? Could be used for snippet names\n\n// Inverted index\n\nCREATE TABLE `index` (\n  `id` int(11) unsigned NOT NULL,\n  `token` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `ext` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `line` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `pos` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `type` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `o_token` varchar(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=latin1;\n\ntruncate `index`;\ninsert into `index` (`id`, `name`, `ext`, `token`, `line`, `pos`, `type`, `o_token`) values\n(4, \'tmap\', \'txt\', \'unicode\', 2, 20, 1, null),\n(5, \'tmap\', \'txt\', \'print\', 2, 15, 1, null),\n(6, \'tmap\', \'txt\', \'1F680\', 2, 25, 1, null);\n\nselect * from `index` where token regexp \'unicide|unicode|unocode\'', '', '', 1, 1500920835097, 0, 4, 0, '1deabcd179d9144febb644df49bab7a8b1714d76bca5b35a132c01f6640e7d0d', '', true, false, '', true, '', false, 0, 1500841410422, 1500841410422, 1500920835097, e'\x1b[0m'),
